ed, oscillating function with\n\n$$\n|9\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|\\le 9.\n$$\n\nHowever, the denominator $4x-1$ grows without bound as $x\\to \\infty .$ So the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1-4x}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{9\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4x-1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see this from the graph of $y=\\frac{-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1-4x},$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951126/assets/64700491874195711ad7291ce0471561df307bd099b5b8a38c33269cf08f21ab.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5414e634-9b33-5dac-9686-4e570efbc7e6" :knowledge-point/title "Comparing an Exponential Function and a Polynomial Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acaf9139-005a-58df-8bf9-ad4672625e2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acaf9139-005a-58df-8bf9-ad4672625e2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264947} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ba83582-b0ea-553c-83fa-8b1421142202" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264946}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6bb37e58-b918-52a6-84b0-b0ce370e540b" :question/math-academy-id "q-310122" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{{x}^{5}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{3x}≫{x}^{5}$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{{x}^{5}}=\\infty .\n$$"}