ac{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see this from the graph of $y=\\frac{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}},$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951126/assets/fd6dbbe8be077ed2eda955802f112540aa8aea73c5c65bae4f0f034176bbdccd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "579373bc-38b3-584c-a118-84be7dfc9074" :knowledge-point/title "Comparing the Relative Magnitude of a Trigonometric Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e92a8c48-b1af-5841-8c49-41167efc5675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e92a8c48-b1af-5841-8c49-41167efc5675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264963} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a5b1e0a-0bc6-5e11-a932-e16aae6ede8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264962}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37ed1105-3f9f-52ba-82e8-30b706cb3bb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-338820" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4x+{x}^{2}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The numerator here is a bounded, oscillating function with \n\n$$\n|-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|\\le 2.\n$$\n\nHowever, the denominator $4x+{x}^{2}$ grows without bound as $x\\to \\infty .$ Since the denominator grows much faster than the (bounded) numerator, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4x+{x}^{2}}=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see this from the graph of $y=\\frac{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4x+{x}^{2}},$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951126/assets/dd869f9140a12c19a0672963c064a4581767a3e39fac8c49b76b6e1067