\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10x)}{2{x}^{3}}-1)=0-1=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5414e634-9b33-5dac-9686-4e570efbc7e6" :knowledge-point/title "Comparing an Exponential Function and a Polynomial Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87b05388-5697-5517-a80c-199ddb2eb2e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264973} {:answer/id #uuid "0d2634a1-0dba-5acf-9813-744ffd122bf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264974} {:answer/id #uuid "cb1e5152-f640-5111-9a9a-afb2edd20017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264975} {:answer/id #uuid "5f91d129-f164-5d89-ae1e-6107bd83eadc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264976} {:answer/id #uuid "01193a55-e7cc-57e1-9735-8803864936a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01193a55-e7cc-57e1-9735-8803864936a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264977} :answer-field/id #uuid "519f3882-c37e-594b-8739-38837a2da5d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264972}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "17d1865b-2f53-5e57-84a7-98e4ef2f19ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-48206" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{2}{e}^{-x}-2).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we can rewrite the first term as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{e}^{-x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{x}}.\n$$\n\nBoth the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{x}≫{x}^{2}$ for large values of $x,$ the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{x}}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{2}{e}^{-x}-2) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{x}}-2 \\\\  & =0-2 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c538b0a9-a084-5a83-a5fa-eca4e0270a93" :knowledge-point/title "Comparing an Exponential Function and a Logarithmic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "070f6020-4cf1-5f58-ab9f-d83d9d077de1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264980} {:answer/id #uuid "73341ef1-954f-575b-810e-5411a67b9185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}{e}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264981} {:answer/id #uuid "407b422a-d523-5b94-a580-e16349709975" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264982} {:answer/id #uuid "2b2c0492-b6d0-5297-a62d-798765ee20e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264983} {:answer/id #uuid "f6377e4d-3644-5f82-8d16-50330b013a64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6377e4d-3644-5f82-8d16-50330b013a64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264984} :answer-field/id #uuid "a253cd3a-0648-557b-b861-c91b0dc22f05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264979}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "112c7ac0-90ce-5a87-a690-2f08cb8f1223" :question/math-academy-id "q-48212" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x){e}^{-x}+5).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we can rewrite the first term as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x){e}^{-x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}{{e}^{x}}.\n$$\n\nBoth the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{x}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)$ for large values of $x,$ the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}{{e}^{x}}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x){e}^{-x}+5) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}{{e}^{x}}+5) \\\\  & =0+5 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "433ac237-32ff-591c-ab0d-e271f5beda30" :knowledge-point/title "Comparing a Polynomial Function and a Logarithmic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f95c6ff-6a39-59a3-94bb-7f134155db4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264987} {:answer/id #uuid "ee25ab9c-b7eb-5b06-907e-f1e97d53c81f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264988} {:answer/id #uuid "5f1b2f05-59d8-54f1-8763-61bb2ecbb23f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264989} {:answer/id #uuid "99f9cec2-09cc-573f-924d-6b5e3afd044e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264990} {:answer/id #uuid "036b5ce7-935c-5bb3-b188-3eba87f740b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "036b5ce7-935c-5bb3-b188-3eba87f740b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264991} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5225af9-3216-505f-8ae1-afca881ac8c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/rad